// auth's inter-service surface: who may use this cloud.
//
// AUTH IS AUTHORIZATION AND IDENTITY, AND NOTHING ELSE. Which repositories make
// a project, and which project a repository belongs to, is the register's
// project table (tau/register/v2): the project id is the author's, from
// project.yaml, and the register is where a link claims it. A project's
// webhook secret and its repositories' deploy keys are the developer's,
// generated by `tau link` and held by the secrets service. Whether a caller
// may write to a repository is the forge's answer, asked by the build
// frontend with the caller's own token, and the tenancy that bounds which
// namespaces a cloud serves is checked there too. Certificates and domain
// claims are the gateway's and pkg/certificate's. None of those is here.
//
